  "corrections_and_boundaries": [
    "Initial old-wrapper probe lacked keep-id mapping and failed before valid reproduction; that failed archive is preserved and not used as data-loss evidence. The corrected three-case old-source probe actually reproduced loss.",
    "The 12 DAGs all succeeded. Their first verifier failed only on integer-versus-double w_neg metadata created from JSON by the reference harness. Strict readback keeps all official score/feature objects unchanged, requires the original exact w_neg value and constructs the longstanding as.numeric(double) wrapper metadata schema. No official estimates, serialized reference files or numerical tolerance were changed and no DAG was rerun.",
    "The hardlink fault suite actually exited zero. Its intentionally shared toy alias initially blocked strict archival. Under its session lease, an explicit maintenance command verified actual inactive unit/MainPID zero and the recorded workspace identity, then materialized the alias as a separate identical-byte regular file. Both evidence-file contents, source code and exit status stayed unchanged; the separate post-terminal receipt is archived. No other directory received deletion authority.",
    "Legacy official_container_v2.R is retained unchanged as historical evidence; its deletion-on-error assertion is obsolete, not a passing current test.",
    "Ordinary inode-checked rollback is proven for injected publication failures, including preserving an unowned replacement; crash atomicity/persistent resume and all-concurrent-worker behavior are not certified."
  ],
